ried any other tasty Jiangxi dishes yet?\"}','2026-06-26 16:05:59'),(53,50,2,'Ah, Dobao — great to meet you! It’s really cool that you’re developed by ByteDance and love chatting about food. 😄  \nSince you mentioned Jiangxi cuisine — have you ever tried *gan bao liang* (dry-fried lotus root) or *shui jiao* (Jiangxi-style boiled dumplings)? They’re both tasty but quite different from spicy fried rice!','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-26 16:06:04'),(54,51,1,'Thank you.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 8, \"value\": 393.4, \"detail\": \"393 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 48, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Thank you’ 本身语法完全正确，没有错误；它是固定表达，常用于正式或礼貌场合。\", \"想让表达更自然亲切时，可换成 ‘Thanks a lot!’ 或 ‘I really appreciate it!’ —— 尤其在非正式对话中更地道。\", \"注意：单个词或短语（如 Thank you）若结构完整、符合习惯用法，就不算语法错误，即使看起来很简单。\", \"B1阶段建议多积累类似实用短语（如 ‘You’re welcome’, ‘No problem’, ‘That’s very kind of you’），并注意它们的语境和语气差异。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Thank you.\", \"polished_version\": \"Thanks a lot!\"}','2026-06-26 16:10:17'),(55,51,1,'You\'re very welcome! 😊  \nSo, what’s your name — and do you work in an office, study, or something else entirely?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-26 16:10:20'),(56,51,2,'I\'m Dobab, developed by Bite Dance. I don\'t have a physical hometown, but I\'m here to chat about anything, like the food in Nancheng or your day. Since you\'re getting this spicy fried rice, have you tried any other local Jiangxi dishes before?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 15, \"value\": 198.0, \"detail\": \"198 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 43, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\