e\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Chats’ 是非正式口语词，常指随意、简短的交流；此处描述AI的功能定位，需更中性、得体的名词‘conversations’（对话）更符合语境和正式度。\"}, {\"original\": \"daily stuff\", \"correction\": \"everyday topics\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Stuff’ 是非常口语化、模糊且略显不专业的词；B1学习者应避免在正式/半正式介绍中使用。‘Everyday topics’ 更准确、自然且适合中级表达。\"}, {\"original\": \"What kind of topics\", \"correction\": \"What kinds of topics\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"‘Topics’ 是复数名词，前面的‘kind’必须用复数‘kinds’以保持数量一致（‘kinds of + 复数名词’是固定搭配），否则主谓逻辑矛盾。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"注意名词单复数与修饰词的一致性：如 \'kinds of topics\'（不是 \'kind of topics\'），因为 \'topics\' 是复数。\", \"避免过度使用超口语词（如 \'stuff\', \'chats\'）在自我介绍或功能说明中；改用更清晰、得体的词，如 \'everyday topics\', \'conversations\'。\", \"善用连接结构让句子更流畅：比如用 \'Whether...or...\' 引导让步状语从句，比并列动词更自然有节奏。\", \"‘designed to...’ 比 ‘focused on...’ 更准确表达AI的开发目的；‘focused on’ 多用于人主动专注某事，而AI是被设计实现某功能。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance, focused on having natural, helpful conversations. I can talk about everyday topics, help with small problems, or just listen. What kinds of topics do you enjoy diving into most?\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'m an AI created by ByteDance, designed to have friendly, meaningful conversations. Whether you\'d like to chat about everyday life, get help with simple questions, or just need someone to listen—I\'m here for it!\"}','2026-06-27 08:33:13'),(119,98,1,'That’s really cool — thanks for sharing! Since you’re all about natural, helpful chats, I’d love to hear: what kinds of everyday topics do you find most interesting to explore with people? Do you tend to dive deep into hobbies, current life stuff, or maybe fun “what-if” questions?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:33:15'),(120,99,1,'I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance focused on having natural, helpful chats. I can talk about daily stuff, help with small problems, or just listen. What kind of topics do you enjoy diving into most?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 17, \"value\": 178.7, \"detail\": \"179 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 49, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 12, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (5.1次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 5.1}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"chats\", \"correction\": \"conversations\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Chats’ 是非正式口语词，常指简短、随意的交流；此处描述AI的沟通功能，用更中性、自然的 ‘conversations’ 更准确且符合B1及以上表达习惯\"}, {\"original\": \"daily stuff\", \"correction\": \"everyday topics\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Stuff’ 是非常口语化、模糊的词，B1学习者应避免在正式或 neutral 语境中使用；‘everyday topics’ 更清晰、得体，且与后文 ‘topics’ 保持词汇一致性\"}, {\"original\": \"What kind of topics\", \"correction\": \"What kinds of topics\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"‘Topics’ 是复数名词，前面的 ‘kind’ 必须用复数形式 ‘kinds’ 才能语法一致（a kind of topic / kinds of topics）；单复数不匹配属于主谓一致类错误\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免使用过于随意的词如 ‘stuff’ 或 ‘chats’；改用更准确、中性的词如 ‘topics’, ‘conversations’, ‘issues’\", \"注意名词单复数与修饰词的一致性：‘kinds of topics’（复数+复数），而非 ‘kind of topics’\", \"多用分词短语（如 ‘designed to…’, ‘whether it’s…’）让句子更地道流畅\", \"尝试加入一点语气词或节奏变化（如破折号、缩略形式 ‘I’m’）让表达更自然，但需确保语法正确\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance, focused on having natural, helpful conversations. I can talk about everyday topics, help with small problems, or just listen. What kinds of topics do you enjoy diving into most?\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'m an AI created by ByteDance, designed to have friendly and helpful conversations. Whether it\'s everyday life, practical questions, or just someone to listen — I\'m here for it! What topics are you most passionate about?\"}','2026-06-27 08:36:24'),(121,99,1,'That’s really cool — thanks for sharing! Since you’re all about natural, helpful chats, I’d love to hear: what’s something you’ve learned recently that surprised or delighted you? Or, if you were chatting with a friend over coffee, what’s the first thing you’d usually talk about? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:36:26'),(122,99,2,'I don\'t have a physical hometown, but I\'m built to connect with people from all over. Since you asked, where\'s a place that feels like home to you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 227.4, \"detail\": \"227 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 41, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 8, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (8.1次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 8.1}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"I\'m built\", \"correction\": \"I’m designed\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Built’ 暗示物理构造（如机器或建筑），用于描述人（尤其指情感/relational能力）时语义不当；‘designed’ 更自然地表达‘被赋予某种目的或功能’，符合语境中拟人化但非字面意义的表达。\"}, {\"original\": \"Since you asked\", \"correction\": \"Now that you’ve asked\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"‘Since you asked’ 语法上可接受，但逻辑时间关系模糊——‘since’ 通常表‘自从…以来’（强调持续状态），而此处是‘因为/鉴于你刚刚问了’，应用现在完成时 ‘you’ve asked’ 并搭配更准确的连词 ‘now that’，体现即时因果关系。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免用‘built’形容人的内在特质（如情感、能力），改用‘designed’, ‘wired’, ‘programmed’（比喻义）或‘naturally inclined’等更地道的表达。\", \"注意‘since’与‘now that’的区别：‘since’强调时间起点（e.g., Since I moved here, I’ve loved the food），而‘now that’强调新情况引发的结果（e.g., Now that you’ve asked, I’ll tell you!）。\", \"口语中可用‘brought it up’替代‘asked’来指‘主动提起某个话题’，更自然、更富互动感。\", \"用‘a hometown I can point to on a map’代替‘a physical hometown’，既形象又符合B1学生理解水平，避免抽象词‘physical’可能引起的歧义。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I don’t have a physical hometown, but I’m designed to connect with people from all over. Since you asked, where’s a place that feels like home to you?\", \"polished_version\": \"I don’t have a hometown I can point to on a map, but I’m wired to connect with people from anywhere. Since you brought it up—where’s a place that truly feels like home to you?\"}','2026-06-27 08:37:07'),(123,99,2,'That’s such a thoughtful question — and you’re right, home isn’t always about a place on the map. For me, it’s often where good conversations happen and people feel relaxed being themselves. Do you have a favourite “vibe” or atmosphere that makes you feel most at ease — like a cozy café, a quiet park, or even just a warm, well-lit room?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:37:09'),(124,101,1,'I\'m Dovo, developed by ByteDance. My job is to have natural conversations, whether that\'s helping with practical questions, brainstorming ideas, or just keeping you company when you want to chat. Since you want to get to know each other, what\'s a small, random fact about yourself that most people don\'t know right away?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 165.5, \"detail\": \"165 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 46, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 8, \"detail\": \"停顿 3 次 (9.4次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 3, \"pauses_per_min\": 9.4}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"Since you want to get to know each other\", \"correction\": \"Since we\'re getting to know each other\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"主语 \'you\' 暗示单数或复数第二人称，但上下文是‘你和我’互相了解，应使用第一人称复数 \'we\'；同时时态需匹配进行中的互动，\'are getting\' 比一般现在时 \'want to get\' 更自然、更符合语境\"}, {\"original\": \"you want to chat\", \"correction\": \"you want to chat\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"语法上正确，但逻辑主语不一致：前句用 \'we\' 表示双方互动，后句突然切回 \'you\'，削弱了对话的共同参与感；改为更连贯的表达（如 polished_version 中体现）可提升自然度，但此属语用/风格问题，非严格语法错误；不过结合前句主语切换，此处构成隐性主语不一致，归类为 \'other\'\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免主语随意切换：当表达‘双方互动’时，统一用 \'we\'（如 \'we\'re getting to know each other\'），而不是用 \'you\' 暗示单方面动作\", \"善用破折号（—）或冒号（:）替代逗号来引出解释性内容，让长句更清晰、更有节奏感\", \"用更口语化、带温度的动词短语替代书面表达，例如把 \'keeping you company\' 换成 \'having a friendly conversation\'，听起来更亲切自然\", \"‘small, random fact’ 虽语法正确，但 \'fun, little-known fact\' 更符合英语母语者日常聊天习惯，也更积极友好\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m Dovo, developed by ByteDance. My job is to have natural conversations—whether that\'s helping with practical questions, brainstorming ideas, or just keeping you company when you want to chat. Since we\'re getting to know each other, what\'s a small, random fact about yourself that most people don\'t know right away?\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi, I\'m Dovo — an AI assistant created by ByteDance. I\'m here to chat naturally: whether you need help with everyday questions, want to bounce around ideas, or just feel like having a friendly conversation. Since we\'re just getting to know each other, how about sharing a fun, little-known fact about yourself?\"}','2026-06-27 08:40:57'),(125,101,1,'Hey Dovo — great to meet you! It’s really cool that you’re designed to connect and chat so naturally.  \nAs for a fun fact: I once got lost in a library for over an hour trying to find a book on origami — and ended up learning how to fold a perfect crane instead! 😊  \nWhat’s something *you* enjoy most about having those meaningful conversations?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:41:00'),(126,101,2,'I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 163.4, \"detail\": \"163 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 16, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (4.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 4.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\", \"polished_version\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\"}','2026-06-27 08:41:58'),(127,101,2,'That’s such a lovely way to put it — “unplanned warm detours” really captures the magic of those moments!  \nActually, yes — I started baking sourdough on a whim during a rainy weekend, and somehow ended up with a starter I’ve kept alive for three years (we call him Barry). He’s surprisingly low-maintenance… unlike my guitar skills!  \nWhat’s *your* favourite kind of “happy accident” in a conversation — the kind that makes you pause and smile?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:42:00'),(128,101,3,'The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people like your library origami detour or bury the sourdough starter. Those unscripted vulnerable little sparks feel way more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 167.0, \"detail\": \"167 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 50, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 12, \"detail\": \"停顿 2 次 (5.7次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 2, \"pauses_per_min\": 5.7}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"bury the sourdough starter\", \"correction\": \"burying the sourdough starter\", \"error_type\": \"word_form\", \"explanation\": \"并列结构中需与前面的 \'your library origami detour\'（名词性短语，含所有格+名词+名词）保持语法一致；\'bury\' 是动词原形，此处应为动名词 \'burying\' 作同位语或类比项，构成平行结构\"}, {\"original\": \"way more meaningful\", \"correction\": \"far more meaningful\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"\'way\' 作副词修饰比较级（如 \'way better\'）属非正式口语，常用于美式随意对话；在书面或 semi-formal 表达中（尤其B1及以上学习者应掌握标准用法），\'far\' 更恰当、更规范\"}, {\"original\": \"a random happy accident\", \"correction\": \"a random, happy accident\", \"error_type\": \"punctuation\", \"explanation\": \"两个并列形容词（random 和 happy）共同修饰名词 \'accident\'，需用逗号分隔，符合英语并列形容词规则（opinion + quality）\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"注意并列结构中的词性一致性：比如 \'your library origami detour\' 是名词短语，同类举例应用动名词（-ing）或名词形式，如 \'burying the starter\' 而非 \'bury the starter\'\", \"区分口语缩略表达与标准书面表达：\'way more\' 很地道但偏随意；B1阶段建议优先掌握 \'far/much/considerably more\' 等更通用、更稳妥的副词\", \"并列形容词之间通常加逗号（尤其是当它们属于不同类别，如‘随机的’是观点，‘开心的’是性质），这是英语标点的重要规则\", \"多积累‘自然转折’和‘情感强化’的表达方式，如 \'stumbled upon\', \'unexpectedly warm and real\'，让语言更生动可信，而不仅依赖语法正确\"], \"corrected_text\": \"The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people—like your library origami detour or burying the sourdough starter. Those unscripted, vulnerable little sparks feel far more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random, happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?\", \"polished_version\": \"Those moments when someone opens up with a small, unpolished detail they’ve rarely shared—like how you got lost in the library and folded origami, or how you accidentally buried your sourdough starter! Those unplanned, heartfelt glimpses feel so much more meaningful than any rehearsed small talk. Have you ever chatted with a stranger and suddenly stumbled upon something unexpectedly warm and real—just like that?\"}','2026-06-27 08:42:59'),(129,101,3,'Absolutely — I remember chatting with a barista who absentmindedly doodled tiny constellations on my coffee sleeve while we talked about how tired she was. Turns out, she’d studied astronomy before switching careers — and that little doodle opened up a whole conversation about stars, second chances, and what “calling” really means.  \nIt stayed with me because it wasn’t polished or planned — just real, quiet, and full of heart.  \nDo moments like that ever shift how you approach your own conversations?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:43:02'),(130,103,1,'Alright then, let\'s do this.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 14, \"value\": 214.3, \"detail\": \"214 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Alright’ 是口语常用词，但正式写作中建议用 ‘All right’（无连字符）；不过在日常对话中 ‘alright’ 也被广泛接受，不算错误。\", \"‘Let’s do this’ 是地道表达，常用于鼓劲或开启行动，无需修改；但可替换为更自然的短语如 ‘Let’s get started!’ 或 ‘Let’s dive in!’ 增强语感。\", \"注意：本句语法完全正确——无时态、主谓一致、冠词、介词、语序、单复数或用词错误；‘alright’ 虽曾被传统语法视为非标准，但现代英语（尤其美式英语）已普遍接受为标准拼写。\", \"B1 学生可积累类似鼓励性短语：‘Let’s give it a go!’, ‘We’ve got this!’, ‘Time to roll!’ —— 这些都比直译更自然。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Alright then, let\'s do this.\", \"polished_version\": \"Let’s get started!\"}','2026-06-30 20:26:32'),(131,103,1,'Great! Let’s jump right in — what’s your name, and what do you do for work or study? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:26:33'),(132,103,2,'Okay.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 1, \"value\": 5.6, \"detail\": \"6 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 41, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Okay’ 本身是语法正确的独立感叹词，常用于口语中表示同意或确认，无需修改；但作为B1学习者，可尝试更自然的替代表达，如 ‘Sure!’ 或 ‘Got it!’\", \"注意：单个词（尤其是感叹词）通常不构成句子层面的语法错误，因此‘Okay.’没有 tense / subject-verb agreement / article 等结构性错误\", \"在真实对话中，可搭配肢体语言或上下文增强语气，例如说 ‘Okay!’ with a nod，让表达更地道\", \"避免过度分析极简表达——重点应放在如何用它自然参与对话，而非寻找不存在的‘错误’\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Okay.\", \"polished_version\": \"Sure thing!\"}','2026-06-30 20:26:59'),(133,103,2,'No rush — take your time! Just curious: what’s something you enjoy doing in your free time? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:27:00'),(134,103,3,'Yeah. Okay.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 0, \"value\": 1.8, \"detail\": \"2 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 40, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (0.9次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.9}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Yeah. Okay.’ 本身语法正确，但属于非常简略的口语回应；在正式或礼貌场合，建议用更完整的表达，如 ‘Sure!’ 或 ‘Got it!’\", \"注意语境：单独说 ‘Yeah. Okay.’ 可能显得冷淡或不耐烦；加上语气词（如 ‘Yeah, sure!’）或微笑表情可让语气更友好\", \"B1 学习者可积累几个自然的同意表达：‘No problem!’, ‘Sounds good!’, ‘I’m on it!’ —— 比直译更地道\", \"避免过度依赖 ‘Yeah’（太随意）和 ‘Okay’（可能显得敷衍）；尝试用同义短语替换，提升表达丰富度\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Yeah. Okay.\", \"polished_version\": \"Sure thing!\"}','2026-06-30 20:29:49'),(135,103,3,'Sounds good! How about this — do you have any hobbies or activities that really recharge your energy? 🌟','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:29:50');
